  "calc": "Method-of-moments Gaussian fit (weighted mean = peak_nm, weighted std = sigma_nm, curve max = amplitude) to the Nikon D700 R/G/B curves in camera-sensitivity-jiang2013.json (Jiang et al. 2013, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). Only the three fitted numbers per channel are original CIE/us-computed statistics of that measured curve, not a reproduction of the table; provided as an unencumbered stand-in wherever the NC-SA restriction on the raw Jiang data is a problem (e.g. a future public/commercial build). It reproduces the real curve's rough shape (peak wavelength and width) but not its fine structure (dual-peak red tail, CFA crosstalk ripple) -- label any use of it 'representative CFA shape, not a measured camera' in the UI.",
